; a `pick` whose condition goes on in the next line, right after a dedent: the dedent closed the two blocks before the tail of the `pick` showed that it needs more input
; (the line was then read again against the blocks that were closed already, "the indentation closes more blocks than are open"; todo 90 a)
load logic, equality
use P c
use ∃ y (P y ∧ y = c)
show A ⇒ A
proof
    assume A
        A
pick y with (P y ∧
        y = c)
    P c
